  "notes": "The source table (Table B-2) provides termination rates by Years of Service only, with no age dimension. The target grid requires rates by Attained Age x Years of Service. Since the source rates are age-invariant (constant across all ages for a given service year), the target rows for ages 25-70 map to the single service-based rate rows. The source table lists specific service years (0-19) and a '20+' bucket. Target columns 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12 map directly to the corresponding service rows. Target columns 30 and 40 map to the '20+' service row. The source values are percentages (e.g., 10.00), so values_unit is 'percent'. No age-specific data exists in the document to differentiate rates by age.",
